{
  "__README": [
    "==========================================================================================",
    "THIS IS THE TEMPLATE. THE FILE THE GATEWAY READS IS identities.json, AND IT IS GITIGNORED.",
    "==========================================================================================",
    "scripts/dev/bootstrap.sh copies this file to identities.json ONCE, if and only if that file",
    "does not already exist, and then rewrites every CHANGE-ME secretKey with a fresh random",
    "value. It never copies over an existing identities.json: that file may hold the credential a",
    "RUNNING gateway is authenticating, and replacing it would split disk from server.",
    "",
    "The rendered identities.json is gitignored because it holds a PLAINTEXT S3 secret key, byte",
    "identical to infrastructure/docker/secrets/s3_secret_key. This template is committed so the",
    "bind source can always be produced on a fresh clone.",
    "",
    "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "WHAT A MISSING identities.json ACTUALLY DOES -- MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED (2026-08-11).",
    "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "The long-standing claim in this repository was that an absent file yields ALLOW-ALL. That is",
    "FALSE for chrislusf/seaweedfs:4.40, which is the tag compose.yaml pins. Measured, each case",
    "started with `server -s3 -dir=/data -s3.config=/etc/s3/identities.json`:",
    "",
    "  bind source absent, so Docker created a DIRECTORY at the path",
    "      F auth_credentials.go:281 fail to load config file ...: is a directory",
    "      -> process EXITS 255. The whole seaweedfs container dies. FAILS CLOSED.",
    "  file present but ZERO BYTES",
    "      F auth_credentials.go:281 unmarshal error: proto: syntax error (line 1:1)",
    "      -> process EXITS 255. FAILS CLOSED.",
    "  -s3.config FLAG OMITTED ENTIRELY",
    "      -> starts cleanly, anonymous ListBuckets returns 200. FAILS OPEN.",
    "  file parses but declares `\"identities\": []`",
    "      -> starts cleanly, anonymous ListBuckets returns 200. FAILS OPEN.",
    "",
    "So the hazard is real but it is NOT triggered by an absent file. It is triggered by dropping",
    "the flag from the command, or by a config that parses to zero identities. Never remove",
    "-s3.config from compose.yaml, and never `echo '{}' >` this path to make a startup error go",
    "away -- that converts a loud crash into a wide-open object store.",
    "",
    "ASSERT IT, DO NOT INSPECT IT. An anonymous ListBuckets against the endpoint must return 403:",
    "    aws --endpoint-url http://127.0.0.1:8333 --no-sign-request s3 ls   # expect AccessDenied",
    "scripts/dev/bootstrap.sh runs this check and fails loudly. The seaweedfs healthcheck in",
    "compose.yaml now also runs it every 15s, so an Allow-All gateway is reported UNHEALTHY and",
    "Traefik-style dependents gate on it, instead of the old probe which only asked the MASTER",
    "whether it was alive and was blind to the S3 gateway's auth posture entirely.",
    "",
    "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "THE SECRETS BELOW ARE PLACEHOLDERS. THEY ARE NOT CREDENTIALS AND MUST NEVER BE DEPLOYED.",
    "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "They are deliberately not base64 and not 32 bytes, so that a template deployed unchanged is",
    "obvious on sight rather than plausible. scripts/ops/preflight.sh fails the deploy on either a",
    "placeholder secretKey or byte-identity with this template.",
    "",
    "NOTE FOR ANYONE ADDING A CHECK: bootstrap.sh rewrites the secretKey VALUES and copies this",
    "prose through untouched, so the placeholder marker string survives into the rendered file by",
    "design. A file-wide `grep -q CHANGE-ME` therefore fires on a CORRECTLY provisioned deploy --",
    "that exact false positive existed and was fixed on 2026-08-11. Anchor any such check to the",
    "\"secretKey\" field, the way preflight.sh now does.",
    "",
    "ACTIONS ARE PER-BUCKET AND PER-PREFIX AND DELIBERATELY NARROW. TENANCY IS NOT ENFORCED HERE:",
    "the org prefix (org/{org_id}/sources/...) is enforced in application code, because a",
    "credential per organization would be a bucket-policy-shaped tenant boundary -- which does not",
    "port to any managed store and is explicitly not the isolation mechanism this system",
    "recognises. These identities separate WORKLOADS, not tenants.",
    "",
    "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "THIS FILE IS READ ONCE, AT GATEWAY STARTUP. EDITING IT CHANGES NOTHING UNTIL A RESTART.",
    "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
    "That gap is a real trap, not a note about caching. Observed live on 2026-08-07: the gateway",
    "had loaded rewritten keys, identities.json was then reverted to this template while the stack",
    "kept running, and everything looked fine -- the application authenticated, anonymous requests",
    "got 403. The damage was queued, not visible: the NEXT restart of `seaweedfs` would have",
    "loaded kb-app as the published placeholder, breaking every object operation the application",
    "makes AND making the repository the only place a working credential exists.",
    "Symmetrical to valkey/users.acl, which was reverted by the same action in the same second;",
    "see infrastructure/docker/valkey/README.md for the same failure written up in full.",
    "So: after ANY change to identities.json, re-run scripts/dev/bootstrap.sh (its rewrite is",
    "idempotent) and assert the running gateway rather than the file -- a signed ListBuckets with",
    "secrets/s3_secret_key must succeed and an unsigned one must return 403. From inside the",
    "`data` network, because this gateway is published on no host port and must never be."
  ],
  "identities": [
    {
      "name": "kb-app",
      "credentials": [
        {
          "accessKey": "kb-app",
          "secretKey": "CHANGE-ME-NOT-A-SECRET-run-scripts-dev-bootstrap-sh"
        }
      ],
      "actions": [
        "Read:kb",
        "Write:kb",
        "List:kb",
        "Tagging:kb"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "__notes": [
    "THERE IS EXACTLY ONE IDENTITY, AND A SECOND ONE WAS REMOVED ON 2026-08-11. This file used to",
    "declare `kb-backup` with ['Read:kb', 'List:kb'] -- read-everything over the whole bucket, in",
    "every organization. Measured before removing it: `kb-backup` appeared in zero lines of",
    "compose.yaml, zero of scripts/ops/preflight.sh and zero of scripts/ops/backup.sh. It had no",
    "consumer at all. scripts/ops/backup.sh does not use the S3 API: it stops the gateway and tars",
    "the `seaweed` VOLUME through a mount (backup.sh, section 2), because there is no consistent",
    "online snapshot of a SeaweedFS cluster and an S3-side copy would also miss the filer",
    "metadata. So the identity was not 'not yet wired' -- the backup method it was named for does",
    "not use credentials.",
    "",
    "Its secret was also the one credential in this repository that no secret sweep could find: it",
    "was generated in bootstrap.sh and written ONLY into the rendered identities.json, with no",
    "twin under infrastructure/docker/secrets/, so every sweep that hashes the files in secrets/",
    "was blind to it by construction. A standing read-everything grant that nothing uses and no",
    "audit can see is a liability, not a spare part.",
    "",
    "IF A BACKUP IDENTITY IS EVER GENUINELY NEEDED (a `weed filer.backup` sidecar to a second",
    "cluster is the production answer backup.sh's header points at), add it together with its",
    "consumer, give it a secrets/ twin so it is sweepable, and extend the identity-set assertion in",
    "scripts/ops/preflight.sh section 6 in the same change. Do not re-add the name alone.",
    "",
    "There is NO admin identity here on purpose. Bucket creation is a one-time operator action",
    "run through `weed shell` on the host, not something an application credential can do -- and",
    "there is exactly ONE bucket, `kb`, forever. Bucket-per-organization multiplies filer",
    "collections without bound, does not port (every managed store caps buckets per account), and",
    "puts a slow quota-governed control-plane operation on the signup path.",
    "",
    "There is no browser-facing identity either, because there are no presigned URLs anywhere in",
    "this codebase. A presigned URL is an unrevokable bearer credential in a URL that lands in",
    "access logs, in Referer and in browser history; it would also require publishing this gateway",
    "as a fifth public hostname in front of a service whose auth fails open. Uploads are",
    "multipart/form-data to Laravel; downloads are a Laravel route that runs the six checks and",
    "streams the response.",
    "",
    "Do not enable bucket VERSIONING. Every DeleteObject would silently become a delete marker,",
    "ListObjectsV2 hides noncurrent versions by design, and the deletion verification pass would",
    "keep reporting clean while the bytes stay on disk.",
    "",
    "The __README and __notes keys are tolerated by the proto unmarshal (verified against 4.40 on",
    "2026-08-11: the real file with both keys loads and the gateway returns 403 to anonymous",
    "ListBuckets). Do not add a key whose VALUE is not a list of strings without re-testing."
  ]
}
